FUCK. The fourteen isn't some mathematical remainder that appeared because we used the wrong operation. It has its own transformation-theoretic identity.\
One caveat: a single outer product \\(I\\otimes O\\) does not contain 49 independently adjustable numbers; it's rank one. The numbers above are dimensions of the spaces spanned by such relationships.\
But I think this is close to what you're reaching for when you talk about the interpretation of the multiplication table evoking latent structure.\
The table gives us a way to take a very ordinary seven-by-seven matrix of relationships and decompose it according to which relationships the cross product expresses directly, and which belong to the algebra's internal symmetry structure.\
We haven't had to assume anything about electrons, gauge forces, or curved spacetime yet.\
Just real vectors and their pairwise products.\
And now I want to do something electromagnetic-looking with them.\
